                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the transformation rule:\n\n1. Identify the most frequent color in the $3 \\times 3$ input grid.\n2. The positions of this color form a $3 \\times 3$ binary pattern/mask.\n3. The $9 \\times 9$ output grid consists of a $3 \\times 3$ tiling of $3 \\times 3$ blocks:\n   - If the corresponding cell in the mask contains the most frequent color, that block is filled with a copy of the full $3 \\times 3$ input grid.\n   - Otherwise, the block is filled with zeros ($0$).",
